JavaScript
JavaScript is an important language for modern web development. It makes websites interactive and dynamic by handling user actions, events and data. 
It provides features like functions, arrays, objects, DOM manipulation and API integration. Overall, JavaScript helps developers build responsive, 
efficient and user-friendly web applications.


React
React.js is a JavaScript library used for building fast, interactive, and dynamic user interfaces. It follows a component-based architecture, 
allowing developers to divide applications into reusable components. React uses JSX to write HTML-like code inside JavaScript. It provides useful features
such as Props, State, Hooks, and Virtual DOM to manage data and update the UI efficiently. Hooks like useState and useEffect help manage component state and
side effects. React also supports routing, API integration, and state management. It makes web development easier, faster, and more organized.





